IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-div-a-employee-employer-contributions`
IMPORT `cp1-div-b-salary-and-wages-contributed-on`

-- Tests of cp1-div-b-salary-and-wages-contributed-on.l4: sections 15, 15.1, 15.2 and 15.3.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text before the file was run. The figures are the illustrative
-- 2024-style figures used in cp1-tests-employee-employer-contributions.l4 (base rate 4.95%, first additional 1%, second
-- additional 4%).
-- Subsection 15(1) read literally: paragraph (b) is AGG - (Xb + (AGG - (Xa + Xb))), which is Xa for any AGG. The cases
-- under "the figure does not depend on what was deducted" assert that reading (NOTES.md, finding).

§ `Tests -- section 15(1)`

-- Args: rate, deducted under this Act, deducted under this Act or a provincial plan, amount of 8(2)(a), amount of 8(2)(b).
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 3_217.5 3_217.5 3_217.5 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000   -- deducted exactly what 8(2)(a) gives: 3,217.50 / 0.0495
-- The figure does not depend on what was deducted (finding).
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 2_000 2_000 3_217.5 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000   -- under-deducted: (a) 2,000 ; (b) 2,000 - (0 + (2,000 - 3,217.50)) = 3,217.50 ; the greater is 3,217.50
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 5_000 5_000 3_217.5 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000   -- over-deducted: (a) 5,000 - 1,782.50 = 3,217.50 ; (b) 3,217.50
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 0 0 3_217.5 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000   -- nothing deducted
-- Part under a provincial plan: 8(2)(a) = 1,398.375 and 8(2)(b) = 1,525.5.
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 1_398.375 2_923.875 1_398.375 1_525.5 EQUALS JUST 28_250   -- (a) 1,398.375 ; (b) 2,923.875 - (1,525.5 + 0)
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (4.95%) 1_600 3_500 1_398.375 1_525.5 EQUALS JUST 28_250   -- excess lies in the provincial deductions: (a) 1,600 - 201.625 ; (b) 3,500 - (1,525.5 + 576.125)
#ASSERT `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` (0%) 1_000 1_000 1_000 0 EQUALS NOTHING   -- a nil rate leaves nothing to divide by
-- Clause 15(1)(b)(ii)(B)
#ASSERT `s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)` 3_500 1_398.375 1_525.5 EQUALS 576.125
#ASSERT `s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)` 3_217.5 3_217.5 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)` 2_000 3_217.5 0 EQUALS (0 MINUS 1_217.5)   -- under-deducted: negative, no floor in the text

§ `Tests -- section 15(1.1) and (2)`
-- Args: year, the employer failed to deduct, the amount that should have been deducted, the date the person notified the Minister.
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 29)) EQUALS JUST 500   -- before June 30 of the following year
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 30)) EQUALS NOTHING   -- June 30 itself is not "before June 30"
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 (JUST (YMD 2024 1 1)) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 (JUST (YMD 2024 7 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 (JUST (YMD 2023 12 31)) EQUALS JUST 500   -- notified in the year itself
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 TRUE 500 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- never notified
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` 2023 FALSE 500 (JUST (YMD 2024 3 1)) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the employer did not fail to deduct
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the first additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 29)) EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the first additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 30)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the first additional contribution` 2023 FALSE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the first additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the second additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 29)) EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the second additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 30)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the second additional contribution` 2023 FALSE 120 (JUST (YMD 2024 6 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the second additional contribution` 2023 TRUE 120 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the base contribution` TRUE 300 EQUALS JUST 300   -- an amount the employer failed to deduct and then pays is deemed deducted
#ASSERT `s 15(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the base contribution` FALSE 300 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.1(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the first additional contribution` TRUE 300 EQUALS JUST 300   -- an amount the employer failed to deduct and then pays is deemed deducted
#ASSERT `s 15.1(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the first additional contribution` FALSE 300 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.2(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the second additional contribution` TRUE 300 EQUALS JUST 300   -- an amount the employer failed to deduct and then pays is deemed deducted
#ASSERT `s 15.2(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the second additional contribution` FALSE 300 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 15.1(1)`
-- Args: rate, deducted under this Act, deducted under this Act or a provincial plan, amount of 8(2)(a.1), amount of 8(2)(c).
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year` (1%) 650 650 650 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year` (1%) 282.5 565 282.5 282.5 EQUALS JUST 28_250   -- (a) 282.5 ; (b) 565 - (282.5 + 0)
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year` (1%) 100 100 650 0 EQUALS JUST 65_000   -- under-deducted: the figure does not depend on what was deducted
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year` (0%) 650 650 650 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c)` 565 282.5 282.5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c)` 700 282.5 282.5 EQUALS 135

§ `Tests -- section 15.2(1)`
-- Args: the ratio of 8(8), rate, deducted (second additional, this Act or a provincial plan), clause 15(1)(b)(ii)(B), clause 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B), the amount of subsection 8(2).
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for a year` 1 (4%) 188 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 4_700   -- one employer: 188 / 0.04
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for a year` (1 DIVIDED BY 2) (4%) 100 10 5 3 EQUALS JUST 1_400   -- ((100 + 10 + 5) - 3) x 1/2 / 0.04
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for a year` 1 (0%) 188 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15.2(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for a year` 1 (4%) 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Tests -- section 15.3`
#ASSERT `s 15.3 — the amount that may be substituted for the aggregate of the amounts deducted by the employer` TRUE 40_000 (4.95%) TRUE EQUALS JUST 1_980   -- 40,000 x 0.0495
#ASSERT `s 15.3 — the amount that may be substituted for the aggregate of the amounts deducted by the employer` TRUE 40_000 (4.95%) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in prescribed circumstances
#ASSERT `s 15.3 — the amount that may be substituted for the aggregate of the amounts deducted by the employer` FALSE 40_000 (4.95%) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no return filed
#ASSERT `s 15.3 — the amount that may be substituted for the aggregate of the amounts deducted by the employer` TRUE 40_000 (1%) TRUE EQUALS JUST 400   -- the rate for the tier concerned
